{"id": "sm2-0351", "domain": "network diagram", "names": ["Core", "Dist", "Acc"], "text": "this is my campus backbone, the plan is to tidy it before the audit. Core feeds Dist and Dist feeds Acc. From now on every new circle should be lime, so the access points stand out. Spawn a circle called Ap next to Acc. Which rules are in force?", "wires": [{"span": "Core feeds Dist and Dist feeds Acc", "trigger": "feeds", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Core,Dist,Acc", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "every new circle should be lime", "trigger": "should be", "type": "rule", "args": {"shape": "circle", "color": "lime"}}, {"span": "Spawn a circle called Ap next to Acc", "trigger": "Spawn", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "create", "shape": "circle", "name": "Ap", "position": "near", "anchor": "Acc"}}, {"span": "Which rules are in force", "trigger": "rules", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "rules"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0352", "domain": "flowchart", "names": ["Intake", "Triage", "Ward", "Home"], "text": "hospital patient flow, hence the serious tone. Intake leads to Triage, then Triage leads to Ward and to Home. Drop the Home to the bottom. Is Home reachable from Intake? And does Triage have a link to Ward?", "wires": [{"span": "Intake leads to Triage", "trigger": "leads to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Intake", "to": "Triage"}}, {"span": "Triage leads to Ward and to Home", "trigger": "leads to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Triage", "to": "Ward,Home"}}, {"span": "Drop the Home to the bottom", "trigger": "Drop", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Home", "position": "bottom"}}, {"span": "Is Home reachable from Intake", "trigger": "reachable", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "path", "from": "Intake", "to": "Home"}}, {"span": "does Triage have a link to Ward", "trigger": "link to", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "connected", "target": "Triage", "anchor": "Ward"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0353", "domain": "mind map", "names": ["Joy", "Fear", "Anger"], "text": "emotions chart inspired by a movie. Joy is yellow, Fear is purple, and Anger is red. Shrink Fear, it's the little one. Does anything touch Joy at the moment? Forget the colour rules I made earlier, they're outdated.", "wires": [{"span": "Joy is yellow", "trigger": "is", "type": "fact", "args": {"target": "Joy", "color": "yellow"}}, {"span": "Fear is purple", "trigger": "is", "type": "fact", "args": {"target": "Fear", "color": "purple"}}, {"span": "Anger is red", "trigger": "is", "type": "fact", "args": {"target": "Anger", "color": "red"}}, {"span": "Shrink Fear", "trigger": "Shrink", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "resize", "target": "Fear"}}, {"span": "Does anything touch Joy", "trigger": "touch", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "neighbors", "target": "Joy"}}, {"span": "Forget the colour rules", "trigger": "Forget", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "forget"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0354", "domain": "cloud architecture", "names": ["Svc", "Db", "Cache"], "text": "quick fix to a diagram I made last week. The plan is to separate read and write paths. Wire Svc to Db and Svc to Cache. Ditch the arrow from Cache to Db if you see one. Swap the Cache and the Db visually, then tell me what the Cache looks like.", "wires": [{"span": "Wire Svc to Db and Svc to Cache", "trigger": "Wire", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Svc", "to": "Db,Cache"}}, {"span": "Ditch the arrow from Cache to Db", "trigger": "Ditch", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "disconnect", "from": "Cache", "to": "Db"}}, {"span": "Swap the Cache and the Db", "trigger": "Swap", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "swap", "target": "Cache,Db"}}, {"span": "tell me what the Cache looks like", "trigger": "looks like", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "describe", "target": "Cache"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0355", "domain": "school diagram", "names": ["Roman", "Greek", "Egypt"], "text": "ancient civilisations timeline. Put Egypt on the left, then Greek, then Roman, in a row. Distribute them evenly. Hmm, label Egypt as Oldest. Is Roman the rightmost? Which one has the most links, if any?", "wires": [{"span": "Put Egypt on the left, then Greek, then Roman, in a row", "trigger": "in a row", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "arrange", "target": "Egypt,Greek,Roman", "layout": "row"}}, {"span": "Distribute them evenly", "trigger": "Distribute", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "distribute", "target": "Egypt,Greek,Roman", "axis": "horizontal"}}, {"span": "label Egypt as Oldest", "trigger": "label", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "label", "target": "Egypt", "label": "Oldest"}}, {"span": "Is Roman the rightmost", "trigger": "rightmost", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "rightmost"}}, {"span": "Which one has the most links", "trigger": "most links", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "mostConnected"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0356", "domain": "game map", "names": ["Hut", "Well", "Tree", "Stone"], "text": "village decorations. Scoot the Well up next to the Hut. Trash the Stone, nobody likes it. Make the Tree green, no wait, lime. Throw two more small lime circles near the Tree, those are bushes. How many circles do we have?", "wires": [{"span": "Scoot the Well up next to the Hut", "trigger": "Scoot", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Well", "position": "near", "anchor": "Hut"}}, {"span": "Trash the Stone", "trigger": "Trash", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "delete", "target": "Stone"}}, {"span": "Make the Tree green, no wait, lime", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Tree", "color": "lime"}}, {"span": "Throw two more small lime circles near the Tree", "trigger": "Throw", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "create", "shape": "circle", "color": "lime", "size": "small", "count": "2", "position": "near", "anchor": "Tree"}}, {"span": "How many circles do we have", "trigger": "How many", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "count", "shape": "circle"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0357", "domain": "org chart", "names": ["Anna", "Bert", "Cleo", "Dan"], "text": "project staffing. Anna and Bert both go to Cleo, so tie them. Cleo goes to Dan. Is there a path from Anna to Dan? Redo the last change, I accidentally undid something. Colour Dan teal.", "wires": [{"span": "Anna and Bert both go to Cleo, so tie them", "trigger": "tie", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Anna,Bert", "to": "Cleo"}}, {"span": "Cleo goes to Dan", "trigger": "goes to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Cleo", "to": "Dan"}}, {"span": "Is there a path from Anna to Dan", "trigger": "path", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "path", "from": "Anna", "to": "Dan"}}, {"span": "Redo the last change", "trigger": "Redo", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "redo"}}, {"span": "Colour Dan teal", "trigger": "Colour", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Dan", "color": "teal"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0358", "domain": "UI wireframe", "names": ["Btn1", "Btn2", "Btn3"], "text": "toolbar sketch. Align Btn1, Btn2 and Btn3 along the vertical, then equalise the gaps. Rename Btn3 to Exit. Is Exit the bottommost? Which one is nearest to Btn1?", "wires": [{"span": "Align Btn1, Btn2 and Btn3 along the vertical", "trigger": "Align", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "align", "target": "Btn1,Btn2,Btn3", "axis": "vertical"}}, {"span": "equalise the gaps", "trigger": "equalise", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "distribute", "target": "Btn1,Btn2,Btn3", "axis": "vertical"}}, {"span": "Rename Btn3 to Exit", "trigger": "Rename", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "rename", "target": "Btn3", "name": "Exit"}}, {"span": "Is Exit the bottommost", "trigger": "bottommost", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "bottommost"}}, {"span": "Which one is nearest to Btn1", "trigger": "nearest", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "nearest", "anchor": "Btn1", "superlative": "closest"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0359", "domain": "family tree", "names": ["Dede", "Papa", "Mama", "Kid"], "text": "my in-laws, as a tree. Dede goes to Papa. Papa and Mama both go to Kid. Slap a small pink star beside Kid, that's the baby. Does Dede touch Kid? Hopefully not directly.", "wires": [{"span": "Dede goes to Papa", "trigger": "goes to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Dede", "to": "Papa"}}, {"span": "Papa and Mama both go to Kid", "trigger": "go to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Papa,Mama", "to": "Kid"}}, {"span": "Slap a small pink star beside Kid", "trigger": "Slap", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "create", "shape": "star", "color": "pink", "size": "small", "position": "near", "anchor": "Kid"}}, {"span": "Does Dede touch Kid", "trigger": "touch", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "connected", "target": "Dede", "anchor": "Kid"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0360", "domain": "sports play", "names": ["Rb", "Wr1", "Wr2"], "text": "offensive formation. Spread Rb, Wr1 and Wr2 evenly across the field, and line them up on one horizontal line. Stick Wr2 in the very back. Then Wr1 should be bigger, enlarge it. Which player is the leftmost?", "wires": [{"span": "Spread Rb, Wr1 and Wr2 evenly across the field", "trigger": "Spread", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "distribute", "target": "Rb,Wr1,Wr2", "axis": "horizontal"}}, {"span": "line them up on one horizontal line", "trigger": "line them up", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "align", "target": "Rb,Wr1,Wr2", "axis": "horizontal"}}, {"span": "Stick Wr2 in the very back", "trigger": "in the very back", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "toBack", "target": "Wr2"}}, {"span": "enlarge it", "trigger": "enlarge", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "resize", "target": "Wr1"}}, {"span": "Which player is the leftmost", "trigger": "leftmost", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "leftmost"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0361", "domain": "pipeline", "names": ["Fetch", "Cache", "Render"], "text": "page load steps. Fetch sends to Cache, Cache sends to Render. Axe the middle one? Heh, no. Make the Cache hexagon-shaped. From now on, whatever I add should be gold. Are Fetch and Render linked directly?", "wires": [{"span": "Fetch sends to Cache, Cache sends to Render", "trigger": "sends to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Fetch,Cache,Render", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "Make the Cache hexagon-shaped", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Cache", "shape": "hexagon"}}, {"span": "whatever I add should be gold", "trigger": "should be", "type": "rule", "args": {"color": "gold"}}, {"span": "Are Fetch and Render linked", "trigger": "linked", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "connected", "target": "Fetch", "anchor": "Render"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0362", "domain": "mind map", "names": ["Sky", "Sea", "Land"], "text": "nature categories. Colour Sky cyan, Sea blue, and Land brown. Duplicate Land twice, it's the biggest. Is Land the biggest? Put Sky above Sea and Sea above Land.", "wires": [{"span": "Colour Sky cyan", "trigger": "Colour", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Sky", "color": "cyan"}}, {"span": "Sea blue", "trigger": "Sea", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Sea", "color": "blue"}}, {"span": "Land brown", "trigger": "Land", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Land", "color": "brown"}}, {"span": "Duplicate Land twice", "trigger": "Duplicate", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "duplicate", "target": "Land", "count": "2"}}, {"span": "Is Land the biggest", "trigger": "biggest", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "biggest"}}, {"span": "Put Sky above Sea", "trigger": "Put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Sky", "position": "above", "anchor": "Sea"}}, {"span": "Sea above Land", "trigger": "above", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Sea", "position": "above", "anchor": "Land"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0363", "domain": "state machine", "names": ["Start", "Mid", "End"], "text": "minimal machine. Link Start to Mid to End, with arrows. Link End back to Start as well. Do we have a cycle now? If yes, delete the link from End to Start. Then is there still a cycle?", "wires": [{"span": "Link Start to Mid to End, with arrows", "trigger": "Link", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Start,Mid,End", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "Link End back to Start as well", "trigger": "Link", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "End", "to": "Start"}}, {"span": "Do we have a cycle now", "trigger": "cycle", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "cycle"}}, {"span": "delete the link from End to Start", "trigger": "delete", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "disconnect", "from": "End", "to": "Start"}}, {"span": "is there still a cycle", "trigger": "cycle", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "cycle"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0364", "domain": "kitchen recipe", "names": ["Rice", "Nori", "Fish", "Soy"], "text": "maki rolls. Put Rice in the center and Nori above it. Tuck Fish and Soy below it, both of them. Hook Fish up to Rice with a plain line. Is the Soy gray? If not, I want it gray.", "wires": [{"span": "Put Rice in the center", "trigger": "Put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Rice", "position": "center"}}, {"span": "Nori above it", "trigger": "above", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Nori", "position": "above", "anchor": "Rice"}}, {"span": "Tuck Fish and Soy below it, both of them", "trigger": "Tuck", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Fish,Soy", "position": "below", "anchor": "Rice"}}, {"span": "Hook Fish up to Rice with a plain line", "trigger": "Hook", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Fish", "to": "Rice", "arrow": "none"}}, {"span": "Is the Soy gray", "trigger": "Is", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "check", "target": "Soy", "color": "gray"}}, {"span": "I want it gray", "trigger": "want", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Soy", "color": "gray"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0365", "domain": "network diagram", "names": ["Mx", "Web", "Db"], "text": "mail and web hosting. Mx connects with Web and Web connects with Db. Which one is the most connected? Is Db the leastConnected one, or is it Mx? Make the winner huge, I mean the most connected one.", "wires": [{"span": "Mx connects with Web and Web connects with Db", "trigger": "connects with", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Mx,Web,Db", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "Which one is the most connected", "trigger": "most connected", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "mostConnected"}}, {"span": "Is Db the leastConnected one", "trigger": "leastConnected", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "leastConnected"}}]}
{"id": "sm2-0366", "domain": "game map", "names": ["Elf", "Troll", "Gate", "Key"], "text": "puzzle level with a gate. Put the Key left of the Gate and the Troll right of the Gate. Is the Key near the Troll? Pop a yellow diamond named Coin above the Key. Throw the Troll to the back, he's hiding.", "wires": [{"span": "Put the Key left of the Gate", "trigger": "Put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Key", "position": "leftOf", "anchor": "Gate"}}, {"span": "the Troll right of the Gate", "trigger": "right of", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Troll", "position": "rightOf", "anchor": "Gate"}}, {"span": "Is the Key near the Troll", "trigger": "near", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "check", "target": "Key", "position": "near", "anchor": "Troll"}}, {"span": "Pop a yellow diamond named Coin above the Key", "trigger": "Pop", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "create", "shape": "diamond", "color": "yellow", "name": "Coin", "position": "above", "anchor": "Key"}}, {"span": "Throw the Troll to the back", "trigger": "to the back", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "toBack", "target": "Troll"}}]}
